  "_comment": [
    "MultiHitBoxLib hitbox profile for orespawn:pitch_black (ENT-S-173, hit boxes that follow the rigs, every species).",
    "Generated by danger.orespawn.tools.hitbox.BossPartProfileWriter from pitchblack.geo.json at the descriptor's adult render scale 1,",
    "rest pose, body yaw 0; 15 parts grouped from the drawn bones by geometry (tools/hitbox_specs_from_rigs.py: touching bones merge while the union stays a compact square-footprint box the cubes fill, tiny bones fold into their neighbours, limb chains merge under the rig's cap, lateral slabs are padded for the flap): each part a box fitted",
    "to the drawn cubes of its member bones, sized [max(x extent, z extent), y extent], synced to its largest member bone, the",
    "pivot taken back through MHLib's rotation so the box sits on the drawn segment. Damage 1.0 on every part: the 1.7.10 mob",
    "was one full-damage box, this aligns the hit boxes with the model and does not rebalance. main-hitbox has no size override,",
    "so the movement and collision box stays Pitch Black's own 2.5x3.5 box times its size tier (PitchBlack.getDefaultDimensions),",
    "not pickable and taking no damage itself: every hit goes through a part. Parts are not solid (a mob is pushed, not stood on)."
